  "why": "DIAGNOSTIC SCREEN (incident P0 not accepted). The same 33 cells as lead-draft-20261013-b. Replay version 3.1 (sim/scenarios/evaluator_IN-26-03365_replay-v3-1.json): seed 2026, compliance 50%, one-stage reopening at 10:00 (clearance 66), 20% of drivers leave at the queue, 6.5 m mean vehicle length, the ramp joining the main line (correction 2). Each other cell changes one of these: seeds 1-5; the reopening as a clearing stage (fast lane at 4.7 km/h 10:00-10:04, slow lane shut) or fully at 10:04 (clearance 70); the ramp as built; compliance 30% and 70% (03-architecture.md section 4); 0, 10, 30 and 40% of drivers leaving; 5 m vehicles. Agreed by the team on 13 October 2026; docs/evaluator-replay-v3-2026-10-13.md gives where each choice comes from.",
  "rule": "A cell counts if its P0 meets the validation targets and none of its runs had a wrong-lane teleport other than at a lane shutting or in a jam; no order is stated if more than 10% of cells do not count. 'A before B' if the 95% confidence interval of the mean of (A delay - B delay) / P0 delay over the counting cells lies wholly below zero; a tie if it contains zero. Validation targets: GEH < 5 in at least 85% of count bins; speed MAPE at most 15% over bins measured at 30 km/h or more; model and detector agree on congested (under 30 km/h) or not in at least 85% of speed bins; no wrong-lane teleport except of a driver stuck from the moment a lane shut or in a jam (a jam teleport on its edge or the next during its wait or the 300 s before) (03-architecture.md section 4, version 2 of 13 October 2026)",
